| `HeroSection`, carousel | home only | Defer until phase 2 home refactor |

## Workflow for each task

1. Pick **one page or one pattern** (not the whole site)
2. Identify existing components/classes that already match the target look
3. Refactor the **canonical page** (Swedish slug, e.g. `paketering/+page.svelte`) — locale wrappers stay untouched
4. Run `npm run format`, then `npm run check` and `npm run lint`
5. Verify visually in the browser
6. Update `todo.md` when done

## Refactoring rules

- **Preserve behavior** — i18n, SEO meta, hreflang, links, and all copy from `src/lib/content/site.js` must stay intact
- **Minimal scope** — do not refactor unrelated pages or rename routes
- **Reuse first** — extend existing components before creating new ones
- **No copy in components** — text stays in `siteContent` / `data.content`; components receive props
- **Unify visuals** — follow the one-visual-treatment principle in `product-design.mdc`

## Suggested page order

| Phase | Pages | Notes |
|-------|-------|-------|
| 1 | `kontakt`, `om-mandalon`, `konsulttjanster`, `kunskapsbank` | Canonical SV pages; EN routes are thin wrappers |
| 2 | `+page.svelte` (home) | Complex — hero, carousel, multiple sections |
| 3 | `designguide` | Large (700+ lines), many bespoke styles — do last |

## Out of scope unless asked

- `analytics_wsgi/` Python backend
- Analytics tracking wiring in `+layout.svelte` (currently commented out)
- TypeScript migration of all route pages
- Route slug or locale structure changes

## Definition of done (per page)

- [ ] Uses shared layout/typography components or global classes consistently
- [ ] No hardcoded user-facing strings (all from `data.content`)
- [ ] Formatted with `npm run format`
- [ ] Passes `npm run check` and `npm run lint`
- [ ] Both SV and EN URLs render correctly
